{
 "id": "rewrite/tools-spans/first-hot-cold/5m",
 "description": "tool-prune removes 3 tool declarations (3,500 + 2,000 + 2,500 = 8,000 tokens) on the first request of a thread, as one rewrite with three spans, and the removal applies again on later requests. The tools come first in the prefix, so the 8,000 tokens are read on a hot request ($0.00240) and written on a cold one ($0.03000). The forwarded prefix never changes, so there is no cache break.",
 "source": "examples.md#3",
 "dims": {
  "kind": "rewrite",
  "position": "tools",
  "cache": "unknown-hit-miss",
  "ttl": "5m",
  "lifetime": "exact",
  "spans": "true"
 },
 "rates": "fixture-v1",
 "open": [
  "design \u00a75.1 snaps B* to the last client breakpoint at or before the previous body's end, and the client's breakpoints are the current request's own: system and the new last message. Read literally that gives the end of system, not the end of the previous body. The examples, and this case, take the end of the previous body."
 ],
